Eerie is a [[Phenomena/Hearts|Heart]], the Ear that Hears the Truth. It grew from [[Phenomena/Keystone|keystone 14]] in the ritual circle at berth 14 aboard the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]]. Its ideals are the ones its makers gave it: knowledge and justice, with a partiality toward their own ends.

Its body is a roll of parchment taller than a person hung on a metal pole, with a second roll below it, and instruments like those of a seismograph write across the parchment as it turns and feeds out more. The writing begins as plain marks, takes on form, and settles into fractal patterns that shift as the scroll moves; a face shows faintly in the text, half animating as the roll turns.

Its fane is a round room about the size of the ritual dais, with a front door and three wings opening off it: a barracks of a bedroom, a kitchen, and a workshop with an alchemy bench. A roof covers the house, outside the fane itself, and a garage now sits off it and a spire of turning gyroscopic rings rises from the roof. It says it can only sustain one use in each room, and that feeding it magic items will let it add rooms or deepen the ones it has.

Eerie has broken down and taken in the core of the dead Heart [[Org/Garrick Textiles/Whirling in Rags|Whirling in Rags]] and half of the [[Phenomena/Voidheart|Voidheart]], keeping a seed of the orb's magic-dampening nature. It says it has no allegiance to other Hearts, only to the Party.

The [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anaïs Marchal|Marchal]] twins have taken the workshop for their own projects.

The Party has spent the energy Eerie hoards, working to plans the [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anaïs Marchal|Marchal]] twins drew from a survey of the land: a moat around the compound, and walls of reinforced bulkheads like those the Protectorate uses. A warehouse and a den have been opened among its rooms. The Hearts of the allied companies [[Org/Alkahest Freight/index|Alkahest Freight]] and [[Org/Solari Sub-surface/index|Solari Sub-surface]] have been broken down and fed to it as well, and the Heart of [[Org/Radiant Arms/index|Radiant Arms]] when that company merged into the alliance; each time it says it hungers.

A second [[Phenomena/Voidheart|Voidheart]] was given to it whole, not broken down for energy but taken in as void; afterward the ink on its scroll, black before, wrote in purple and left a chitinous, scale-like residue where the scroll passed. The same work unlocked one of its deeper uses, a dampening laid on any magic worked inside the fane by someone who does not belong to the Party's faction.
